{
  "unit": {
    "id": "es-a2-u03",
    "title": "-ER / -IR preterite",
    "subtitle": "The completed past of -er and -ir verbs: Anoche comí en casa",
    "level": "A2",
    "order": 3,
    "xp_reward": 20
  },
  "grammar": {
    "title": "One set of endings for two verb families",
    "intro": "You've done the past of <b>-ar</b> verbs — now finish the job with <b>-er</b> and <b>-ir</b>. The great news: in the preterite they share <b>exactly the same endings</b>. Learn them once and you can say <i>comí</i>, <i>viví</i>, <i>escribí</i>, and <i>salí</i>. Keep an eye on the accents in <b>comí</b> and <b>comió</b> — they carry the stress.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "tag": "terminaciones",
        "heading": "The shared -er / -ir endings",
        "body": "Drop the <b>-er</b> or <b>-ir</b> and add these endings. The accents on the <b>yo</b> and <b>él/ella</b> forms are essential — they mark the stress:",
        "conj": [
          [
            "yo",
            "comí"
          ],
          [
            "tú",
            "comiste"
          ],
          [
            "él/ella",
            "comió"
          ],
          [
            "nosotros",
            "comimos"
          ],
          [
            "vosotros",
            "comisteis"
          ],
          [
            "ellos",
            "comieron"
          ]
        ],
        "ex": [
          {
            "es": "Anoche <b>comí</b> en casa.",
            "en": "Last night I ate at home.",
            "note": "yo → comí (accent!)"
          },
          {
            "es": "Él <b>comió</b> pizza.",
            "en": "He ate pizza.",
            "note": "él/ella → comió"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "tag": "ir-verbos",
        "heading": "-IR verbs use the very same endings",
        "body": "There's no separate set for <b>-ir</b> verbs in the preterite — <b>vivir</b>, <b>escribir</b>, and <b>salir</b> take the identical endings you just learned:",
        "conj": [
          [
            "vivir → yo",
            "viví"
          ],
          [
            "escribir → yo",
            "escribí"
          ],
          [
            "salir → yo",
            "salí"
          ]
        ],
        "ex": [
          {
            "es": "<b>Escribí</b> una carta anoche.",
            "en": "I wrote a letter last night.",
            "note": "escribir → escribí"
          },
          {
            "es": "<b>Salí</b> con mis amigos.",
            "en": "I went out with my friends.",
            "note": "salir → salí"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "tag": "acentos",
        "heading": "The accent marks the person",
        "body": "The accent tells you <b>who</b> and <b>when</b>. <b>Comí</b> is 'I ate', <b>comió</b> is 'he/she ate'. Say <b>come</b> with no accent and you're back in the present:",
        "conj": [
          [
            "he/she eats (now)",
            "come"
          ],
          [
            "I ate",
            "comí"
          ],
          [
            "he/she ate",
            "comió"
          ]
        ],
        "ex": [
          {
            "es": "Yo <b>comí</b> a las dos.",
            "en": "I ate at two.",
            "note": "yo → comí"
          },
          {
            "es": "Ella <b>comió</b> tarde.",
            "en": "She ate late.",
            "note": "él/ella → comió"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "takeaways": [
      "-er/-ir preterite endings: -í, -iste, -ió, -imos, -isteis, -ieron.",
      "-er and -ir verbs share the exact same endings: comí, viví, escribí, salí.",
      "Use it for completed past actions: Anoche comí en casa.",
      "Mind the accents: comí (I ate) vs comió (he/she ate) vs come (present)."
    ],
    "mistakes": [
      {
        "w": "Anoche yo comé en casa.",
        "r": "Anoche yo comí en casa.",
        "why": "The -er/-ir yo ending is -í, not -é: comí, not comé."
      },
      {
        "w": "Ella comio tarde.",
        "r": "Ella comió tarde.",
        "why": "The él/ella form needs the accent: comió, not comio."
      },
      {
        "w": "Anoche salió con mis amigos.",
        "r": "Anoche salí con mis amigos.",
        "why": "For 'I went out' use salí; salió is he/she went out."
      }
    ]
  },
